535403 true] [17592186347467 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347468 13194139535403 true] [17592186347467 1089 "q-110600" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347467 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535403 true] [17592186347467 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/assets/815f5ce1dd5bf3bc30b7853b53cd97736ffeb8224f30bc864cc7e43e07bedb5a.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347467 1113 #uuid "8507283e-b6bb-5932-a798-405f13041eec" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347467 1145 "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents a set that does not contain the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\"" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347469 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347470 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347471 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347472 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347473 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1041 "selection" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347472 13194139535403 true] [17592186347468 1110 #uuid "c11c39a3-1a92-52c7-a05a-0f6c1920d5f0" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347469 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347469 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347469 1111 #uuid "84151b21-6f86-5a8f-aa97-e624b37808e3" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347470 1034 "I only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347470 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347470 1111 #uuid "fbda7dc0-e7f5-5bf8-a648-bceda7dad6b5" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347471 1034 "III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347471 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347471 1111 #uuid "6a914d9c-5401-5fa1-b1c5-9f0e1a1053c6" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347472 1034 "None" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347472 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347472 1111 #uuid "6052102f-7783-591d-9aeb-d17a0642bc80" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347473 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347473 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347473 1111 #uuid "05413364-8482-521e-a9a6-20b4e06c8cd5" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347474 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347475 13194139535403 true] [17592186347474 1089 "q-110611" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347474 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535403 true] [17592186347474 1100 "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:xyz=1}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x+y-z=0}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:y=-1}$" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347474 1113 #uuid "2f7eefdd-4562-5d0a-9cb1-c1a07721f95b" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347474 1145 "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $xyz=1$ since $0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x+y-z=0$ since $0+0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $y=-1$ since $0\\ne -1.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347476 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347477 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347478 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347479 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347480 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1041 "selection" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347480 13194139535403 true] [17592186347475 1110 #uuid "a8879922-bb8a-5f15-ad55-70d6d2a97517" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347476 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347476 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347476 1111 #uuid "672bfc64-fc1b-5c48-97ab-eda6ca11974a" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347477 1034 "I only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347477 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347477 1111 #uuid "bf59cbe1-fcfa-5bbb-a07e-2e57ffc9ecc6" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347478 1034 "III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347478 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347478 1111 #uuid "eb99172f-5a1e-5b34-a0b5-8a275f34e668" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347479 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347479 1111 #uuid "dc8e330c-accc-5a71-a770-4ad6fc6e6dc0" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347480 1034 "II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347480 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347480 1111 #uuid "542ec833-404f-5ad9-8e01-09c8df03924e" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347481 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347482 13194139535403 true] [17592186347481 1089 "q-110760" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347481 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535403 true] [17592186347481 1100 "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x-4y=1}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x=-2y}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0}$" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347481 1113 #uuid "d2f09bfc-d5e1-5138-8cc9-33a8e30bda91" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347481 1145 "Let's analyze each subset.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. For instance, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $x-4y=1$ since $0-4\\cdot 0=0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x=-2y$ since $0=-2\\cdot 0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. No point in ${R}^{3}$ satisfies the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0.$ Hence, $C=∅.$ The empty set is not a subspace since it does not contain the zero vector.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347483 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347484 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347485 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347486 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347487 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1041 "selection" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347487 13194139535403 true] [17592186347482 1110 #uuid "f28a8b77-8231-5720-9ee8-cabc25da699d" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347483 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347483 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347483 1111 #uuid "18cc4f6d-6456-5a28-ac40-984297c1a92b" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347484 1034 "I only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347484 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347484 1111 #uuid "e8ecbd8d-4951-5118-b33f-625f599c022d" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347485 1034 "III 