rue] [17592186347524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347528 13194139535403 true] [17592186347524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347529 13194139535403 true] [17592186347524 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535403 true] [17592186347524 1041 "selection" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347524 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347526 13194139535403 true] [17592186347524 1110 #uuid "ec52a9b5-d9f9-589a-b1ea-9aed3cc42a0f" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347525 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347525 1111 #uuid "bc2b0312-e1a3-58c2-b94e-0c67abde35c4" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347526 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347526 1111 #uuid "aae593b1-e75d-5fec-9fd9-bca17dd77d2c" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347527 1034 "I only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347527 1111 #uuid "1ff94b71-9f03-54aa-a3b3-54325a27df0e" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347528 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347528 1111 #uuid "91fb9ec6-6879-50c1-a7aa-7d354a15aad9" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347529 1034 "II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347529 1111 #uuid "d5ac0df7-7dce-58f4-843b-7cc6c9921a86" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347531 13194139535403 true] [17592186347530 1089 "q-35600" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347530 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535403 true] [17592186347530 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/assets/ec79ffa15b3ed25d8f439f575e1cdffc3122ae1d82e1b55500a6e5e2e17cf4fc.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347530 1113 #uuid "985b4894-28d8-5dc3-a41a-ba282ffe63f1" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347530 1145 "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace.  Every subspace must contain the origin,  but from the diagram, we can easily see that the origin is not in the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents a subspace. It represents the whole plane, which is considered a special subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$  without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347532 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347533 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347534 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347535 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347536 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1041 "selection" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347536 13194139535403 true] [17592186347531 1110 #uuid "47692804-81b4-54ad-b1d6-9b943810f370" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347532 1034 "I only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347532 1111 #uuid "bd277386-d90f-5ff0-b0eb-4ea1b93b1766" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347533 1034 "III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347533 1111 #uuid "2da251fc-63ec-55b2-80df-2661ea4c6ede" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347534 1034 "None" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347534 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347534 1111 #uuid "d5368ab0-8ae9-589b-863f-36f997f2f7d7" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347535 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347535 1111 #uuid "90aaf807-947a-52ea-bb57-030154d8bf8d" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347536 1034 "II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347536 1111 #uuid "8fe93e33-098b-513b-ae76-0596a5a0c13a" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347537 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347538 13194139535403 true] [17592186347537 1089 "q-74217" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347537 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535403 true] [17592186347537 1100 "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:1-x-y=0}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 1}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:2x+3y-z=0}$" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347537 1113 #uuid "65e032cf-8dda-5eb9-b8c9-342357ab6106" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347537 1145 "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $1-x-y=0$ since $1-0-0\\ne 0.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace. Indeed, the vector $u=⟨1,0,0⟩$ is in $B$, but $2u=⟨2,0,0⟩$ is not in $B$, since ${2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}≰1.$ So, $B$ is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- The set $C$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $2x+3y-z=0$ since $2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $C.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347539 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347540 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347541 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347542 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347543 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1041 "selection" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347541 13194139535403 true] [17592186347538 1110 #uuid "db84572d-151c-52ee-8d3d-8a3d74303cfa" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347539 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347539 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347539 1111 #uuid "283d9b5b-fa77-5dd1-917e-aeba63cc6db8" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347540 1034 "I only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347540 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347540 1111 #uuid "2da680ee-7912-5815-ab67-dc610d8c26f2" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347541 1034 "III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347541 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347541 1111 #uuid "19bbfa69-c2f1-574e-8f8b-32fb296a7af1" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347542 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347542 1111 #uuid "8473034b-5111-50da-a03f-842d6e9efe9d" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347543 1034 "II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347543 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347543 1111 #uuid "c166fdb4-a774-59a2-a9dc-2b1bd5315fe3" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347544 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347545 13194139535403 true] [17592186347544 1089 "q-74218" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347544 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535403 true] [17592186347544 1100 "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:xyz=0}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:y=-1}$" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347544 1113 #uuid "cb5240e2-b91f-57ca-8218-7498b10038ab" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347544 1145 "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ since ${0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace because it is not closed under vector addition. Indeed, both $a=⟨1,0,1⟩$ and $b=⟨0,1,1⟩$ belong to $B$ but \n\n$$\na+b=⟨1,0,1⟩+⟨0,1,1⟩=⟨1,1,2⟩\n$$\n\n \ndoes not satisfy the condition $xyz=0$ since $1\\cdot 1\\cdot 2\\ne 0.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $y=-1$ since $0\\ne -1.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\"" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347546 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347547 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347548 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347549 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347550 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1041 "selection" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347548 13194139535403 true] [17592186347545 1110 #uuid "0fda5663-6ca0-57e8-ba77-a2145fb06cb6" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347546 1034 "I only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347546 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347546 1111 #uuid "a21df31e-2fcb-580b-9c42-0723d6014f5a" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347547 1034 "III only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347547 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347547 1111 #uuid "2324473b-3b0a-5672-b74a-70e479023dfb" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347548 1034 "None" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347548 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347548 1111 #uuid "4dc65f3f-f060-5c8f-8456-4043fa543989" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347549 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347549 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347549 1111 #uuid "f2897c60-481b-52e0-b8b3-905e3398f8cd" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347550 1034 "II only" 13194139535403 true] [17592186347550 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535403 true] [17592186347550 1111 #uuid "61307106-65e0-5ca5-8c49-99b4fe624265" 13194139535403 true]] :edb/te